ng  around the country trying to make the  case to be elected as president well I  think that quote was a little bit out of  context but let me ask you a question I  am enormous ly proud of the fact that we  have the most diverse progressive  freshmen  in the history of the United States  Congress and you know what I did in 2016  and in 2018 I ran all over this country  to try to make that happen  all right so when you talk about the  political revolution you're talking  about two things number one are the  ideas that we are fighting for an  economy that works for all not just the  1% but the second point that I have made  over and over again is we're not going  to be able to implement a progressive  agenda unless millions more people get  involved in the political process yeah  so Bernie answers it perfectly well he  then goes on to say it was very painful  that those allegations were made okay  very quickly people started looking  around and saying okay shadi and Assad  it says on CNN that she's an American  University student turns out she's a  public policy intern at this lobbyist  Cassady and associates and people were  able to confirm this by looking at her  LinkedIn Cassady and associates is an  establishment DC lobbying firm it's  connected to Democratic Minority Leader  Harry Reid's former deputy chief of  staff former Minority Leader who's  currently the CEO they worked for the  Egyptian government to improve Egypt's  image in the u.s. after news of Egyptian  human rights abuses surfaced they were  actually sort of involved in a number of  different political issues and the  argument was this is a plant from an  establishment firm to smear Bernie with  this question but it's not totally clear  that that's when it was the other  argument that has been made is this was  someone who simply teed up for Bernie a  really great opportunity to deal with  the sexual assault sexual harassment  allegations so the question really for  me is are these individuals being  presented in the way that most reflects  their presence at the Town Hall I'll  give you some other examples of this  here's one other one Tara Eversole okay  Tara Eversole was listed as a former  biology professor when she asked a  question if you look at her LinkedIn  profile yes she used to be a bi all  professor but right now she's the chair  of the Baltimore County Democratic Party  she's a political operative she's not  just some random former biology  professor now does that tell us whether  her presence is in order to antagonize  Bernie from an establishment point of  view or to help Bernie no it doesn't it  just tells us that the room is filled  with political operatives rather than  just random disinterested voters other  than wanting to figure out who to vote  for another example a woman named Avena  McAllister Avena McAllister presented as  a mother of two and I'm sure she is a  mother of two but according to the  Charles County Democratic Central  Committee website  she is a democratic committee member she  has a formal position within a local  Democratic Party and I could go on and  on and on there's a whole long list of  these so the question is what does it  matter what does it matter  initially the allegation was CNN  participated in stacking the room with  anti Bernie people to smear him then  people started thinking a little bit  more in a nuanced way about this and  what is the most likely scenario to me  Pat and you tell me if you disagree is  that anytime there's one of these town  halls everybody who has an interest and  that is going to be disproportionately  political groups political operatives  lobbyists etc they try to get their  people in the room obviously they would  try to do that so I think that if  anybody is at fault here it's number one  CNN for maybe not doing enough to get  actual just regular voters in the room  and number two the titles that these  people were assigned I think are  deceptive I totally agree I blame CNN  not getting the right titles or at least  the appropriate titles and I think we  are on edge here and we have the right  to be because Bernie Sanders was screwed  in 2016 not just by the DNC but also by  the establishment media right they  didn't cover his rallies at the  beginning they didn't cover his campaign  meanwhile they were covering Donald  Trump's empty podium and you know had  plenty of interest in Hillary Clinton so  we don't want to see that happen again  in 2020  no and I think a lot of the discussion  about this is wrongly about debating the  merits of a question about sexual  assault because as soon as you argue  that this was a planted shill from a  lobbying group to smear Bernie about  sexual assault  you then have to defend that the sexual  assault questions not valid and while I  agree that sadena Saabs framing was not  a complete framing sexual assault in  campaigns particularly if you're talking  about women's rights and gender equality  it's a perfectly legitimate question so  for me it's less about pointing to that  question as a smear or a softball I  don't know exactly what that particular  lobbying firms interests are in this  election they may well be establishment  and they may be trying to hurt Bernie or  not I just don't know we don't know  exactly what their role is right now  this is sort of breaking news how  candidates deal with sexual assault  matters the question was incorrectly  framed Bernie Sanders answered the  question to the best of his ability  overall what we have to understand is  that this is calculated theater for  television and the sources that have  money are going to disproportionately  have control over the discourse that's  really the message CNN has an interest  in selecting from the questions that are  submitted the ones that they think are  going to be most interesting and  relevant and Cain's a case in point this  question from a lobbyist in turn was  selected to be clipped separately on  CNN's website so CNN has 